## Findings: How Nebula & MiraAPI Display Role Name + Task Count

### 1. NEBULA — Role Name on Player Name Tags (in-world, above player model)

**File:** `D:\API参考\Nebula-Public-master\Nebula-Public-master (1)\Nebula-Public-master\Nebula\Patches\UpdatePatch.cs`

**WHERE:** On the **player model's name text** (`player.cosmetics.nameText`), updated **every frame** in `HudManager.Update` → `ResetNameTagsAndColors()`.

**HOW the text is built:**

```csharp
// Base: playerData.currentName (the actual player name)
player.cosmetics.nameText.text = playerData.currentName;

// If observer can see everyone's info, append the original name in gray:
if (CanSeeEveryoneInfo && currentName != originalName)
    player.cosmetics.nameText.text += Helpers.cs(new Color(0.65f,0.65f,0.65f), $" ({playerData.name})");

// Append role suffix via role's EditDisplayName / EditOthersDisplayName:
player.cosmetics.nameText.text += " " + name;
```

The `name` variable is built via two callbacks:
```csharp
Helpers.RoleAction(player, (role) => { role.EditDisplayName(player.PlayerId, ref name, hideFlag); });
Helpers.RoleAction(PlayerControl.LocalPlayer, (role) => { role.EditOthersDisplayName(player.PlayerId, ref name, hideFlag); });
```

These add **rich-text colored symbols** or text. For example, the **Lover role** (`Roles/ExtraRoles/Lover.cs`) appends:
```csharp
displayName += Helpers.cs(iconColor, "♥");  // <color=#RRGGBBAA>♥</color>
```

**WHEN updated:** Every frame via `HudManager.Update` Postfix.

**Color of the name text:**
```csharp
// Self: use role's color
if (player == PlayerControl.LocalPlayer)
    player.cosmetics.nameText.color = playerData.role.Color;
// Others: white by default
else
    player.cosmetics.nameText.color = Color.white;

// Then override for impostor detection
player.cosmetics.nameText.color = rewriteImpostorColor(playerData, current, impostorColor);

// Then let each role modify the color
Helpers.RoleAction(player.PlayerId, (role) => { role.EditDisplayNameColor(player.PlayerId, ref color); });
Helpers.RoleAction(PlayerControl.LocalPlayer.PlayerId, (role) => { role.EditOthersDisplayNameColor(player.PlayerId, ref color); });
```

---

### 2. NEBULA — Role Name + Task Count in a Secondary Info Label (below name)

**File:** `D:\API参考\Nebula-Public-master\Nebula-Public-master (1)\Nebula-Public-master\Nebula\Patches\PlayerControlPatch.cs`

**WHERE:** On a **separate "Info" TextMeshPro** childed under `p.cosmetics.nameText.transform`, positioned below the name.

**HOW it's built (method `UpdateAllPlayersInfo()`):**

```csharp
// Create or find a child "Info" text under nameText
Transform playerInfoTransform = p.cosmetics.nameText.transform.FindChild("Info");
if (playerInfo == null) {
    playerInfo = Object.Instantiate(p.cosmetics.nameText, p.cosmetics.nameText.transform);
    playerInfo.fontSize *= 0.75f;  // smaller font
    playerInfo.gameObject.name = "Info";
}
playerInfo.transform.localPosition = new Vector3(0f, 0.5f / 2.8f, 0f);
```

The text is formatted as:

```csharp
// Role name (rich-text colored)
if (data.ShouldBeGhostRole)
    roleNames = Helpers.cs(data.ghostRole.Color, roleName);
else
    roleNames = Helpers.cs(data.role.Color, roleName);

// Task count (only for local player or if can see everyone's info)
string taskInfo = tasksTotal > 0
    ? HasFakeTask
        ? $"<color=#868686FF>({completed}/{total})</color>"        // gray for fake tasks
        : $"<color=#FAD934FF>({completed}/{total})</color>"        // yellow for real tasks
    : "";

// Final info text (local player sees role on first line, + task info)
playerInfo.text = $"{roleNames} {taskInfo}".Trim();
```

For the **local player only**, the task tab header is also updated:
```csharp
if (p == PlayerControl.LocalPlayer) {
    TextMeshPro tabText = TaskPanelBehaviour.Instance.tab.Find("TabText_TMP").GetComponent<TextMeshPro>();
    tabText.SetText($"{TranslationController.Instance.GetString(StringNames.Tasks)} {taskInfo}");
}
```

**WHEN updated:** Every `FixedUpdate` of `PlayerControl` (via `PlayerControlPatch.Postfix`), but only for the **local player** loop (`if (__instance.PlayerId == PlayerControl.LocalPlayer.PlayerId)`).

---

### 3. NEBULA — Task Panel Text (role hint + task list)

**File:** `D:\API参考\Nebula-Public-master\Nebula-Public-master (1)\Nebula-Public-master\Nebula\Patches\RoleInfoPatch.cs`

**WHERE:** In the **task panel** (`TaskPanelBehaviour`), patched via `TaskPanelBehaviour.SetTaskText` Postfix.

**HOW it's reformatted:**

```csharp
// Prepend: colored role name + hint
string text = Helpers.cs(role.Color,
    Language.GetString("role." + role.LocalizeName + ".name") + ": " +
    Language.GetString("role." + role.LocalizeName + ".hint"))
    + "\n" + __instance.taskText.text;

// Append custom role-specific task text
string? append = data.role.GetCustomTaskText();
if (append != null) text += "\n" + append;

__instance.taskText.text = text;
```

**WHEN updated:** Whenever `TaskPanelBehaviour.SetTaskText()` is called by the game (typically when task list changes or panel opens).

**Role can suppress task display** via `ShowTaskText` property:
```csharp
public virtual bool ShowTaskText => true;  // Roles can override to false
```
And provide custom task text via:
```csharp
public virtual string? GetCustomTaskText() => null;
```

---

### 4. NEBULA — Meeting Screen Name Display

**File:** `D:\API参考\Nebula-Public-master\Nebula-Public-master (1)\Nebula-Public-master\Nebula\Patches\UpdatePatch.cs` (lines 220-255)

**WHERE:** In `MeetingHud.Instance.playerStates`, each `PlayerVoteArea.NameText`.

**HOW it's built:**

```csharp
string prefix = "<line-height=80%>";
string name = "";
Helpers.RoleAction(player.TargetPlayerId, (role) => { role.EditDisplayName(player.TargetPlayerId, ref name, false); });
Helpers.RoleAction(PlayerControl.LocalPlayer, (role) => { role.EditOthersDisplayName(player.TargetPlayerId, ref name, false); });
if (!name.Equals(""))
    player.NameText.text = prefix + playerData.name + " " + name;
else
    player.NameText.text = prefix + playerData.name;
```

Color is set with same logic (self = role color, others = white, then modified by roles).

The info sub-text (role name + task count) is also added under meeting names via `UpdateAllPlayersInfo()`:

```csharp
Transform meetingInfoTransform = playerVoteArea.NameText.transform.parent.FindChild("Info");
if (meetingInfo == null) {
    meetingInfo = Object.Instantiate(playerVoteArea.NameText, playerVoteArea.NameText.transform.parent);
    meetingInfo.transform.localPosition += Vector3.down * 0.10f;
    meetingInfo.fontSize *= 0.60f;
}
meetingInfo.text = $"{roleNames} {taskInfo}".Trim();
// Hidden during results screen
if (meetingInfo != null) meetingInfo.text = MeetingHud.Instance.state == VoteStates.Results ? "" : meetingInfoText;
```

---

### 5. MIRAAPI — Role Name Display

**Source found at:** `D:\API参考\MiraAPI-master\MiraAPI-master\MiraAPI\` and partial source in `D:\API参考\MiraAPI部分源码.txt`

**MiraAPI does NOT appear to handle role name display on player models.** The partial source code (19,566 lines) covers:
- Plugin loading (`MiraApiPlugin.cs`, `MiraPluginManager`)
- Options system (`ModdedOptionsManager`, `ModdedNumberOption`, `ModdedEnumOption`, etc.)
- Custom game modes (`CustomGameMode`)
- Custom game endings (`CustomGameOver`)
- Custom colors (`CustomColor`, `PaletteManager`)
- Modifiers system
- Networking (RPCs for syncing options)
- UI helpers (buttons, settings tabs, HUD positioning)

**No patches for `cosmetics.nameText`, `SetName`, `TaskPanelBehaviour`, or role name display on players.** MiraAPI provides infrastructure for mod developers to build their own role system — it does not include a built-in role display implementation.

---

### 6. VANILLA Among Us Behavior (from combined_code.txt)

**File:** `D:\C#解决方案与.cs\AssemSDKAU\combined_code.txt`

**`PlayerCosmetics.SetName()`** (line ~104761):
```csharp
public void SetName(string nameStr) {
    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(nameStr))
        this.nameText.text = TranslationController.Instance.GetString(StringNames.PlayerName);
    else
        this.nameText.text = nameStr;
}
```
Also has overloads: `SetName(string, Vector3 scale, Color color, float zPosition)`.

**`PlayerNameColor`** static class (line ~180490):
```csharp
public static Color Get(NetworkedPlayerInfo pc) => Get(pc?.Role);
public static void Set(PlayerControl pc) => Set(pc, pc.Data?.Role);
private static Color Get(RoleBehaviour role) => role?.NameColor ?? Color.white;
```

This is called by `PlayerControl.RpcSetName` → `CoSetName` → `RawSetName` → `cosmetics.SetName(name)` and `cosmetics.SetNameMask(true)`.

**`TaskPanelBehaviour`** (line ~212229):
```csharp
public void SetTaskText(string str) {
    this.taskText.text = str;
}
```
Vanilla game calls this with `PlayerControl.LocalPlayer.Data.Tasks.ToArray()` formatted text. There is no role name or hint — just raw task list.

The panel position floats at the left-top of screen, with `openPosition.y = 0.6f` (normal) or `1.6f` (Hide & Seek).

---

### Summary Table

| **Aspect** | **Vanilla AU** | **Nebula (Player Model)** | **Nebula (Info sub-text)** | **Nebula (Task Panel)** | **MiraAPI** |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Role on name tag?** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes (colored suffix) | ✅ Yes (below name, 0.75× size) | ✅ Yes (role name + hint prepended) | ❌ Not handled |
| **Task count on name tag?** | ❌ No | ❌ No | ✅ Yes `(0/3)` colored | ✅ Yes (original task list below) | ❌ Not handled |
| **Update timing** | On SetName | Every `HudManager.Update` (~60fps) | Every `PlayerControl.FixedUpdate` | When `SetTaskText` is called | N/A |
| **Rich text?** | ❌ Raw text | ✅ `<color=#RRGGBBAA>` | ✅ `<color=#RRGGBBAA>` | ✅ `<color=#RRGGBBAA>` | N/A |
| **Meeting screen role?** | ❌ No | ✅ Role suffix on `NameText` | ✅ Role+task below name (0.6× size) | N/A | N/A |

### Key Code Reference Locations

| What | File | Lines |
|---|---|---|
| Nebula: per-frame name tag update | `Patches/UpdatePatch.cs` | 130-210 |
| Nebula: info sub-text (role+task below name) | `Patches/PlayerControlPatch.cs` | 270-340 (`UpdateAllPlayersInfo`) |
| Nebula: task panel role hint | `Patches/RoleInfoPatch.cs` | 18-50 (`TaskTextPatch`) |
| Nebula: `ShowTaskText` / `GetCustomTaskText()` | `Roles/Role.cs` | 120, 224 |
| Nebula: `EditDisplayName` virtual methods | `Roles/Assignable.cs` | 616-668 |
| Nebula: `Helpers.cs` rich text color | `Helpers.cs` | 255-258 |
| Vanilla: `PlayerCosmetics.SetName` | `combined_code.txt:104761-104770` | 104761-104770 |
| Vanilla: `PlayerNameColor` | `combined_code.txt:180490-180552` | 180490-180552 |
| Vanilla: `TaskPanelBehaviour.SetTaskText` | `combined_code.txt:212229-212348` | 212229-212348 |

